                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Bottom line: 5/10, love the art style, story was pleasant and tied things up neatly, puzzles are such that you can semi-shut your brain off to play (perfect for winding down after work), game length is pleasant too, but gameplay was buggy. Get it on discount. To the team: please make more games and get even better!\n\n(Gotta admit I wouldn't have bought this if I didn't know Alasdair Beckett-King worked on this. Followed him on YouTube for awhile. That said; I've got no regrets going through this game.)\n\nPros: I have a soft spot for an art style like this. I really like the backgrounds the game has. Have screenshotted a couple to use as wallpapers.\n\nThe puzzles are pretty alright, and don't suffer from classic point-and-click jank (pixel-hunting, item combinations that make zero sense). The fact you can highlight everything that's interactable is a huge plus (I thank you for respecting my time). Tbh I had to read a walkthrough at a couple points, but I'll chalk that up to a skill issue than a game design issue.\n\nI think the writing was pleasantly decent. A simple story of.. maybe I shouldn't spoil it? But it was a nice, simple story. Predictable twist, but eh it's not a big deal; it's not like the game set out to be some grand epic. I didn't notice any potholes nor left with any unanswered questions. Enjoyed all the characters both major and minor. The jokes were good, too!\n\nCons: the game can get buggy, but never enough to be written-off. There's noticeable things like Harper's sprites being on a lower layer than some but not all background sprites, and only for certain sprites of his? The game also gets increasingly laggy between screen transitions and when opening up sub-inventories the longer I keep it running, to the point I've had to quit and reopen the game multiple times in a playthrough. I *am* playing this on (I'm sorry) Linux, so it could just be Linux Issue. I hope (not sorry) Windows users don't face the same thing.",
